(c) Implementation details
We trained the proposed model and the baselines by utilising the AdamW optimizer with a Mean Square Error (MSE) loss function and a batch size of 128 (Loshchilov and Hutter, 2018). Moreover, we applied an exponential learning rate decay schedule with an initial rate of 0.001 and decaying every 6000 steps with a base of 0.9, alongside a fixed weight decay with 0.001. All the experiments were conducted on the platform equipped with an AMD Ryzen 7950x CPU and a single NVIDIA 4090 GPU.
